# The qualifier move over a real corpus, both ways.  What this adds over the
# mini_repo round trip is the variety: qualifiers on template arguments, on
# nested argument lists that close with `>>`, next to a member function's own
# `const`, and spelled through macros -- the cases where "which `const` is
# this" is decided by something other than the two tokens next to it.
#
# Measured (2026-09-13, fastbuild tool, 48 cc_* targets, 88 files touched):
#   east  4688 edits, rebuild 0m14s, converge 2m40s
#   west  4697 edits, rebuild 0m14s, converge 3m05s
#   ~11 min total.  The reverse leg finds 9 more edits than the forward one
#   produced, because it also moves the qualifiers googletest already wrote
#   east.
#
# No EXPECT_ROUNDTRIP_IDENTICAL.  The two directions cancel out on everything
# either of them moved, but the moved run is re-emitted with single spaces, so
# a qualifier originally written `const    int` comes back as `const int`.
# That is a formatting difference the round trip cannot undo, and on a corpus
# this size it is not worth asserting the absence of; `rebuild2` and
# `converge2` are the assertions that matter.
REPO=googletest
RULESET=east_const
RULESET_THEN=west_const
EXPECT=pass
